function portPrompt(p, base) {
  return `${COMMON}
TASK (M2-R9 port, key ${p.key}; your base commit is ${base}: your work so far is git diff ${base} in ${REPO}): ${p.scope}${RESUME[p.key] ? '\n' + RESUME[p.key].note : ''}
DONE WHEN: ${p.done}.
Report: ${REPO}/docs/m2-r9-${p.key}.md (what changed and why, file by file; each Cataclysm delta with its exe function and address; the build results; the plain-harness runs with label, milestone and first stop; the new or extended self-test; the generator and how to rerun it; delta-map review entries you added; the CAT-TODOs you closed or re-targeted; every stream hash before and after with the fields and first tick that moved; for producer 1 the replay comparisons led by their headlines; for the mission producers a per-mission table (mission, objectives N/M in order, done tick, stream hash, pair) and the generator's verification counts; for producer 4 the recording's files and the user's GOG playback steps; a "For STATE.md" list of chosen names and defaults; what is left and its owner). Subsystems: split your scope into 3-6 subsystems and record them in the done marker.
Return via StructuredOutput: report, files_changed, summary, done_when_met, harness_milestone, first_stop, stream_hash_after (the sha256 prefix of your final mission run's run.hwo), counts, open_questions, and missions_passed (the mission numbers whose self-test passed as a byte-identical pair, if your scope has any).`
}

function auditPrompt(p, r, base) {
  return `${COMMON}
TASK: ADVERSARIAL AUDITOR for M2-R9 port "${p.key}" (producer result: ${JSON.stringify(r || {}).slice(0, 2500)}). RESUME RULE: if ${REPO}/docs/audits/m2-r9-${p.key}.md exists and ends with a "Verdict:" line, return its numbers immediately.
1. Build from clean in a separate dir: rm -rf ${SCRATCH}/build-audit-r9-${p.key} && meson setup / compile the debug and release configurations there exactly as tools/build.sh does (read it), 0 warnings under -Werror; record sizes.
2. ${p.audit}
3. Read the full diff of this port: git diff ${base} in ${REPO} (the commits after ${base}, WIP snapshots included, plus the working tree; commits whose subjects show they are the user's or the orchestrator's, such as harness rules, asset tools, oracle sessions, the play-test launcher, merges or workflow relaunches, are not port work). Every change outside the producer's scope, every edited function the delta map calls IDENTICAL without a review entry, every Cataclysm change without a "CAT:" comment, every CAT-TODO not on one line with its owner first, every stream move the producer did not state, every generated file that a rerun of its generator does not reproduce is a finding.
4. Re-check the producer's DONE WHEN claim (${p.done}) yourself on the plain harness (silent, through tools/m2_harness.sh only).
Fix factual errors you prove directly (code or doc; mark doc fixes "[audit: ...]"), keep the build green, and count the fixes. Write ${REPO}/docs/audits/m2-r9-${p.key}.md: what you checked, each finding with evidence, precision = correct/(correct+wrong) over the sampled checks, fixes, the mission-stream hash your final pair gave and every other guard-rail stream you reran (the next port's reference), and a last line "Verdict: PASS|PASS-WITH-FIXES|FAIL - <reason>".
Then CHECKPOINT this port (even on FAIL, so the next port starts from a recorded state): ${CKPT} "M2-R9 ${p.key}: <verdict word> (<one-line summary>)" (it refuses forbidden paths; on an index.lock, wait 30 s and retry). Return the commit hash in "commit".`
}

